sections.text:
The most common error is poor field notes: missing dates, missing instrument names, or figures that cannot be read later.

Other frequent mistakes are:
mixing degrees, minutes and seconds with decimal degrees;
forgetting to record temperature and pressure for electronic distance measurement;
using the wrong datum or projection and then mixing coordinates from different systems;
mis-identifying a station, so angles are booked to the wrong point;
applying a correction with the wrong sign;
trusting software output because it looks precise.

Also state your assumptions and show the check. An examiner needs to see how you reached the answer, not only the answer.
